    "text": "The market repriced U.S. monetary policy expectations sharply higher after stronger-than-expected economic data, with the Federal Reserve's next move now viewed as potentially a rate hike rather than a cut. Thursday's PCE inflation data and jobless claims represent extremely high-impact releases that will drive volatility, with geopolitical developments also a potential catalyst. USD/JPY continues to rise steadily supported by strong U.S. labour market data, with quotes at 159.93 approaching levels of previous interventions. The biggest wildcard remains potential dramatic developments between the USA and Iran which could override data flows and trigger sharp repricing across FX and commodities.",
